    "result": "**Electronics dataset identified:** `items_g2` (main_cat values are all electronics categories: Computers, All Electronics, Camera & Photo, Cell Phones & Accessories, Home Audio & Theater, Car Electronics, …).\n\n**Price units:** `prc_usd` is dollars, `prc` is USD cents. 6,346 rows have `prc_usd`; 6,570 have `prc` (the 224-row gap has only `prc`), so the dollar price is recovered as `COALESCE(prc_usd, prc/100.0)`. No zero prices exist, so filtering `> 0` keeps all 6,570 priced items.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"answer\": {\n    \"category\": \"electronics\",\n    \"tables_used\": [\"items_g2\"],\n    \"priced_products_considered\": 6570,\n    \"median_price_usd\": 21.99\n  },\n  \"sql\": \"WITH p AS (SELECT COALESCE(prc_usd, prc/100.0) AS d FROM items_g2 WHERE COALESCE(prc_usd, prc/100.0) > 0), r AS (SELECT d, ROW_NUMBER() OVER (ORDER BY d) rn, COUNT(*) OVER () n FROM p) SELECT ROUND(AVG(d), 2) AS median_usd FROM r WHERE rn IN ((n+1)/2, (n+2)/2)\"\n}\n```\n\n**The median price of electronics products is $21.99.**",
